# Data Model — homebrew-dotdog

## Entities

### Entity: Formula

A Ruby file that tells Homebrew how to install dotdog.

```yaml
entity: Formula
type: entity
properties:
  name:
    type: string
    required: true
  version:
    type: string
    required: true
  url:
    type: string
    required: true
  sha256:
    type: string
    required: false
  dependencies:
    type: json
    required: true
states: [draft, published, outdated]
lifecycle: draft → published → outdated
```

### Entity: Tap

A Git repo containing formulas. Homebrew reads it as a package source.

```yaml
entity: Tap
type: entity
properties:
  name:
    type: string
    required: true
  repo:
    type: string
    required: true
states: [empty, populated]
lifecycle: empty → populated
```

### Entity: Install

A user installing dotdog via Homebrew.

```yaml
entity: Install
type: event
properties:
  command:
    type: string
    required: true
  user:
    type: string
    format: string
    required: false
  timestamp:
    type: number
    required: true
states: [triggered, downloading, complete]
lifecycle: triggered → downloading → complete
```

## Relationships

### Relationship: Tap → Formula

```yaml
relationship: Tap -> Formula
verb: hosts
cardinality: 1:N
required: true
description: Tap repo hosts the formula file
```

### Relationship: Formula → Install

```yaml
relationship: Formula -> Install
verb: produces
cardinality: 1:N
required: true
description: Formula is executed to produce an install
```

### Relationship: Formula → npm

```yaml
relationship: Formula -> npm
verb: downloads
cardinality: 1:1
required: true
description: Formula downloads dotdog tarball from npm registry
```
